{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". Count sequences with no run of 3 same bits. This is classic Fibonacci-like. Let a_n be number of length n strings with no 000 or 111. We can use recurrence: Let f(n) be total. We can use state machine with last two bits. Let's compute via DP.\n\nDefine states: last two bits pattern: 00,01,10,11. But need to avoid 000 and 111. So if last two bits are 00, next bit cannot be 0 (would make 000). So next must be 1. Similarly for 11 cannot add 1. For 01 and 10, both next bits allowed.\n\nLet dp[n][state] counts length n ending with that state. For n=2, initialize: 00:1, 01:1,10:1,11:1.\n\nFor n>2, transition: new state determined by last two bits of new string. For each previous state, add next bit b, produce new state = last bit of prev + b.\n\nCompute iteratively up to n=14.\n\nLet's do quickly.\n\nn=2: dp2 = {00:1,01:1,10:1,11:1}\n\nn=3: compute dp3.\n\nFrom state 00: next bit cannot be 0, so b=1. New state = 01. add 1 to dp3[01].\nFrom 01: b can be 0 or1. b=0 -> new state 10. add1. b=1 -> new state 11. add1.\nFrom 10: b can be 0 or1. b=0 -> new state 00. add1. b=1 -> new state 01. add1.\nFrom 11: b cannot be1, so b=0. new state 10. add1.\n\nSum: dp3[00]=1, dp3[01]=1+1=2, dp3[10]=1+1=2, dp3[11]=1. total=6.\n\nn=4: dp4.\n\nInitialize zeros.\n\nFrom 00 (1): b=1 -> state01 add1.\nFrom 01 (2): each count 2. For each: b=0 -> state10 add2. b=1 -> state11 add2.\nFrom 10 (2): b=0 -> state00 add2. b=1 -> state01 add2.\nFrom 11 (1): b=0 -> state10 add1.\n\nTotals: state00:2, state01:1+2=3, state10:2+1=3, state11:2. total=10.\n\nn=5: dp5.\n\nFrom 00 (2): b=1 -> state01 +2.\n01 (3): b0 -> state10 +3; b1 -> state11 +3.\n10 (3): b0 -> state00 +3; b1 -> state01 +3.\n11 (2): b0 -> state10 +2.\n\nTotals: state00:3, state01:2+3=5, state10:3+2=5, state11:3. total=16.\n\nn=6:\n\nFrom 00 (